WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
10,000 people signed up in 15 days for five treatments the FDA has not approved. This is Peptides Weekly Episode 10. Education and Evidence, never dosing advice. After that launch, a medical association's objection to wider unapproved peptide access, a real-world look at glp-1 drugs and alcohol, and Terry Paratide, a parathyroid fragment with actual fracture trials. Hymns and hers, Journal Arta and Parataban reported, put a specialty called Peptides Plus on 6.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:33.240
sale in the United States on November 18th, 2026.

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:36.620
The offering is a commercial launch, not a trial result.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:43.340
The five compounded products are Sermore Ellen, Glutothione, NAD Plus, Vitamin B12, and

00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:48.720
L-Carnitine, prepared by licensed United States pharmacies that state pharmacy boards inspect.

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:51.300
A wait list had opened in late October.

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:56.640
Chief Medical Officer Anna Vinjamori said the company does not have the data clinicians

00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:01.320
are used to having with compounds like this, and that people with serious cardiovascular,

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:07.700
liver, or kidney disease will not be candidates for now. Joshua Critzer, a chemist at Tufts,

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:12.320
said that without large trials, it is hard to rule out rare serious complications,

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:16.980
and that anecdotal information is not enough reason to put a substance in your body.

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:23.340
Paul Notephler at UC Davis called dosing a separate uncertainty. The company also plans to add

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:30.340
BPC 157 and TB 500, two peptides marketed for healing, though most of the research on

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:32.280
them is in animals rather than people.

00:01:33.262 --> 00:01:38.482
The American Medical Association has opposed a health and human services proposal to expand

00:01:38.482 --> 00:01:42.442
access to unapproved peptides, Florida Hospital News reported.

00:01:43.162 --> 00:01:48.402
That objection comes after federal officials, earlier this month, moved to widen compounding

00:01:48.402 --> 00:01:50.462
access to those same kinds of products.

00:01:50.462 --> 00:01:55.402
The Washington Times added that health professionals are sounding the alarm on the policy.

00:01:55.922 --> 00:02:01.062
This is a professional and political response, not a new study of whether any peptide works.

00:02:02.311 --> 00:02:07.331
GLP1 drugs turn up in a side post report on a real-world study that links them with less

00:02:07.331 --> 00:02:10.491
alcohol use and with eating the outlet calls healthier.

00:02:11.111 --> 00:02:12.711
That is an observation in people.

00:02:13.251 --> 00:02:17.711
It is not a randomized trial, and a link is not proof the drugs caused either change.

00:02:17.711 --> 00:02:24.351
weight loss GLP1 prescriptions paid by Medicaid fell after four states withdrew coverage, two-minute

00:02:24.351 --> 00:02:29.551
medicine reported, which is a before and after pattern in who gets a prescription. Health

00:02:29.551 --> 00:02:34.291
day casts the same drop as Medicaid cuts causing prescriptions to plummet, a harder

00:02:34.291 --> 00:02:39.171
causal claim than a coverage withdrawal by itself can carry. Australia has approved

00:02:39.171 --> 00:02:44.251
or for glipron, streamlined feed reported, and the approval is for the country's first

00:02:44.251 --> 00:02:50.991
non-peptide oral GLP1 pill. Same hormone pathway, different kind of molecule. This one is not

00:02:50.991 --> 00:02:57.093
a peptide. Terry Paratide, this week's spotlight, is recombinant human parathyroid hormone.

00:02:57.693 --> 00:03:04.813
Amino acids 1-34. A 2005 review in Endocrine reviews put it in an anabolic class for severe

00:03:04.813 --> 00:03:10.653
osteoporosis. A drug with a chance to change bone micro-architecture, set against medicines

00:03:10.653 --> 00:03:13.233
that mainly slow breakdown and cut remodeling.

00:03:13.573 --> 00:03:16.253
The clinical reviews talk about daily treatment.

00:03:16.613 --> 00:03:19.953
A 2016 paper in osteoporosis international

00:03:19.953 --> 00:03:23.213
reported that Terry Paratite appears to raise bone formation

00:03:23.213 --> 00:03:25.993
more than bone resorption on blood markers

00:03:25.993 --> 00:03:27.233
and on tissue slides.

00:03:27.793 --> 00:03:29.013
Two things happen together.

00:03:29.553 --> 00:03:31.613
Formation is stimulated inside sites

00:03:31.613 --> 00:03:34.133
that are already remodeling and on surfaces

00:03:34.133 --> 00:03:35.173
that had been quiet.

00:03:35.753 --> 00:03:37.813
New remodeling sites also start up.

00:03:37.813 --> 00:03:41.273
Both feed the density gains seen on DXA scans.

00:03:41.693 --> 00:03:46.453
Remodeling is the repair cycle that keeps bone young, and under this drug each of those

00:03:46.453 --> 00:03:51.533
cavities is described as finishing in positive bone balance, which the authors treated as

00:03:51.533 --> 00:03:53.233
one reason fractures might fall.

00:03:53.773 --> 00:03:58.713
The same review said fracture risk does fall, and that the effect looks larger as therapy

00:03:58.713 --> 00:03:59.673
goes on longer.

00:04:00.173 --> 00:04:05.333
It judged a full continuous 24-month course better for skeletal outcomes than shorter stretches,

00:04:05.333 --> 00:04:11.153
and said novel shorter regimens should wait for controlled trials against that 24-month daily course.

00:04:11.713 --> 00:04:15.513
Clinical use that paper stated is limited to 24 months.

00:04:16.153 --> 00:04:23.233
In 2016, the authors called it the only agent then available that builds new bone and can partly repair architectural defects.

00:04:23.773 --> 00:04:26.313
That exclusivity belongs to the date of the paper.

00:04:26.853 --> 00:04:33.753
The strongest fracture evidence in this set is a Phase III trial, summarized in that 2005 endocrine reviews paper.

00:04:33.753 --> 00:04:38.833
Elderly women who already had at least one vertebral fracture had significant reductions

00:04:38.833 --> 00:04:41.713
in spine fractures and in fractures of the limbs.

00:04:42.293 --> 00:04:47.213
The review said there was not yet evidence those reductions beat bisfosfinates and cost

00:04:47.213 --> 00:04:50.873
utility estimates found teraparitide significantly more expensive.

00:04:51.493 --> 00:04:57.453
A separate 2005 health technology assessment pulled in 90 randomized trials covering elendronate,

00:04:57.453 --> 00:05:03.173
Atidrinate, recedrinate, reloxaphine, and teraparitide among other comparators.

00:05:03.633 --> 00:05:08.633
All five of those drugs had cut vertebral fracture risk in women with severe osteoporosis

00:05:08.943 --> 00:05:10.593
and adequate calcium intake.

00:05:11.093 --> 00:05:15.473
Head-to-head comparisons had not shown anyone significantly more effective than the others.

00:05:15.973 --> 00:05:20.313
In the cost model, the price of a quality adjusted life year fell sharply with age.

00:05:20.833 --> 00:05:26.213
At age 50, assuming severe osteoporosis right at the diagnostic threshold, nothing in

00:05:26.213 --> 00:05:30.313
When the model came in under 35,000 pounds per quality adjusted life year.

00:05:30.833 --> 00:05:37.053
At age 60, reloxofine was estimated at 26,000 pounds if hip fractures were unaffected and

00:05:37.053 --> 00:05:39.373
31,000 if the hip effect was harmful.

00:05:39.993 --> 00:05:43.373
And the authors said those figures were driven by breast cancer assumptions.

00:05:43.853 --> 00:05:48.053
No other option in that model was under 35,000 pounds at age 60.

00:05:48.593 --> 00:05:52.713
A 2026 paper in regenerative therapy is a different kind of result.

00:05:52.713 --> 00:05:59.133
Researcher's built mouse bone marrow exosomes carrying teraparitide messenger RNA, and coated

00:05:59.133 --> 00:06:02.953
them with an ASP-6 peptide meant to stick to hydroxyapatite.

00:06:03.393 --> 00:06:09.013
In mouse stromal cells, that package raised teraparitide message and secreted protein, switched

00:06:09.013 --> 00:06:15.093
on a CRE-linked reporter, and increased osteogenic genes, alkaline phosphatase staining and

00:06:15.093 --> 00:06:16.073
mineral in the matrix.

00:06:16.693 --> 00:06:19.773
It bound bone samples more tightly than plain exosomes.

00:06:19.773 --> 00:06:25.173
After an intravenous injection, fluorescence on bone was still detectable at 72 hours,

00:06:25.593 --> 00:06:30.133
stronger in the femur and tibia and relatively weaker in the liver than with unmodified

00:06:30.133 --> 00:06:30.833
exosomes.

00:06:31.573 --> 00:06:35.293
Cell work and mouse bio-distribution, not a human fracture trial.

00:06:35.793 --> 00:06:41.373
The 2005 review said terror paratite is not recommended beyond two years, in part because

00:06:41.373 --> 00:06:44.713
a rat carcinogenicity model produced osteosarcoma.

00:06:44.713 --> 00:06:50.393
It discussed the drug for postmenopausal women and men with severe osteoporosis, for

00:06:50.393 --> 00:06:55.313
established steroid-related osteoporosis when steroids have to continue, and for some

00:06:55.313 --> 00:06:59.373
people under 65 with a T score of minus 3.5 or lower.

00:06:59.993 --> 00:07:01.433
That is what the review considered.

00:07:01.893 --> 00:07:04.213
It is not a reason to start or stop anything.

00:07:04.753 --> 00:07:09.493
The same review treated mild high blood calcium as something that can show up and that clinicians

00:07:09.493 --> 00:07:10.333
then managed.

00:07:10.333 --> 00:07:17.773
A 2026 case report in bone reports, one patient described an impending atypical femoral fracture

00:07:17.773 --> 00:07:20.753
on the opposite side after a single denosa mab dose.

00:07:21.433 --> 00:07:25.033
The other femur had looked normal on imaging when the first fracture happened.

00:07:25.553 --> 00:07:29.833
The patient had long bisfosfinate exposure and had not finished teraparitide.

00:07:30.273 --> 00:07:34.933
The authors called atypical femoral fracture a rare but serious complication of prolonged

00:07:34.933 --> 00:07:40.313
anti-resorptive therapy, and they called the risk of teraparitide followed by an anti-resorptive

00:07:40.313 --> 00:07:45.973
of drug poorly characterized. Across these papers, teraparitide is an established bone-building

00:07:45.973 --> 00:07:51.913
medicine with a 24-month clinical limit and phase 3 fracture data in older women. They

00:07:51.913 --> 00:07:56.633
do not show it prevents more fractures than bisfosvenates, and the exosome experiments

00:07:56.633 --> 00:08:01.723
do not show a result in people. What is worth knowing is that a real-world link between

00:08:01.723 --> 00:08:07.763
GLP1 drugs and less drinking or different eating is a pattern in people, not proof the medicine

00:08:07.763 --> 00:08:12.683
and caused it. A drop in Medicaid prescribing after coverage disappears shows how payment

00:08:12.683 --> 00:08:17.883
rules change who receives these drugs, not whether they work. And a fracture result from

00:08:17.883 --> 00:08:22.203
a randomized trial in women who already had a spine fracture sits in a different evidence

00:08:22.203 --> 00:08:24.943
class from a compounded product sold without approval.

